{
  "name": "Reference to Video - MiniMax H3",
  "author": "InvokeAI",
  "description": "Generate video+audio conditioned on reference media with MiniMax H3 Ref2VA.",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "contact": "",
  "tags": "minimax h3, text to video, video, audio",
  "notes": "Condition a new clip on reference media: wire up to 3 Video Reference and up to 9 Image Reference nodes through chained Collect nodes into BOTH the Reference Conditioning node and the Prompt node - the same ordered references must reach both, and reference ORDER changes the result. A video reference can contribute its image track, its soundtrack, or both (soundtrack-only references must be paired with at least one visual reference).\n\nNumber of Frames appears twice: the Denoise node's dropdown and the integer field feeding the Prompt and Reference Conditioning nodes. They must match; the run stops with a clear error if they do not.\n\nSelect the Ref2VA transformer (e.g. 'MiniMax H3 Ref2VA Transformer (int8, pruned)') in the model loader's Transformer field - the FL2VA transformer cannot consume references.\n\nEach InvokeAI install assigns its own internal model IDs, so every model field ships blank -- pick your installed models in the form before invoking.",
